# Elixir test files, or single tests, that cannot pass on beamlet by design. tools/elixir-tests
# reports them separately. One per line: FILE[:TEST NAME] then the reason after " -- ".
# (tools/elixir-tests.skip.<engine> lists those that hold with only one regex engine.)
application_test.exs:application directory -- expects Elixir compiled inside its source checkout
code_test.exs -- inspects BEAM's code_server process, which does not exist here
kernel/cli_test.exs -- runs the elixir and iex executables (the real BEAM) by shell command lines naming the VM's paths, which the host's shell does not see
kernel/dialyzer_test.exs -- runs dialyzer, an OTP tool not run here
system_test.exs:argv/0 -- runs bin/elixir (the real BEAM) by a shell command line naming a VM path, which the host's shell does not see
system_test.exs:os signals -- sends a Unix signal to the VM's own OS process; OS signals are not delivered to the VM
port_test.exs:info/1,2 with registered name -- opens a UDP socket (gen_udp); the VM has no UDP
file_test.exs:cp cp_r skips sockets and other special files -- creates a Unix-domain socket (gen_tcp, local); the VM has none
kernel/errors_test.exs:macros error stacktrace -- known: frames of macros run by erl_eval differ (not by design; open)
kernel/errors_test.exs:macros interpreted function clause stacktrace -- known: as above (open)
exception_test.exs:binary constructor error info on binary concatenation -- error message detail for binary construction not reproduced
